# Technology stack

Read `docs/TECH_STACK.md` before changing repository tooling, package management, build, tests, docs, release infrastructure or major dependencies.

Baseline direction:

- Bun workspaces; no pnpm/yarn/npm lockfile.
- Vue 3.5 stable baseline; do not move the default runtime to a prerelease.
- TypeScript 7 stable is the canonical compiler baseline.
- An isolated TypeScript 6 compatibility bridge is allowed only for Vue tooling that cannot yet consume TypeScript 7; never silently downgrade the project baseline.
- Biome 2.5+ is the sole lint/format tool. Do not add ESLint, TypeScript ESLint or Prettier without an explicit project-level decision.
- Enable Biome's Vue recommended domain and Vue/HTML-like full support; use narrow Biome overrides for real tool false positives.
- Vite 8 is the library/build tool.
- Vitest + Vue Test Utils are the test baseline; use browser-mode tests selectively for real browser behavior.
- Storybook with Vue/Vite is the component development environment.
- VitePress stable is the public docs system.
- Plain CSS + `--dui-*` variables; no core Tailwind/UnoCSS/CSS-in-JS dependency.
- No Reka UI or other component/headless framework.
- Floating UI DOM may be added only when overlay positioning work requires it.
- `vue-component-meta` is the first choice for generated public API metadata; isolate legacy compiler compatibility if it needs it.
- Changesets is the planned monorepo release/versioning tool.
- MCP later uses the stable `@modelcontextprotocol/server` v2 line and local stdio first.
- GitHub Actions + Pages/Releases are the infrastructure baseline; no required VPS.

Do not add Turborepo, Nx, Lerna, tsup, unbuild, Sass, ESLint, Prettier, another test runner or another build system without a concrete demonstrated requirement and an explicit project-level decision.
